# Local development values, loaded by `npm run server`. Production sets real environment variables instead:
#   NODE_ENV=production
#   FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=<real project id>   (do NOT set the *_EMULATOR_HOST variables)
#   CORS_ORIGINS=https://<your-hosting-domain>   (comma-separated, https only)
#   VOUCHER_ENCRYPTION_KEY=<openssl rand -base64 32>   (required; encrypts demo Wi-Fi voucher passwords at rest)
#   APPROVAL_SECRET=<openssl rand -base64 32>   (required; keys approver one-time codes and sessions)
#   APP_BASE_URL=https://<your-hosting-domain>   (required; where approval links in emails point)
#   MAIL_TRANSPORT=smtp, SMTP_HOST, SMTP_PORT, SMTP_USER, SMTP_PASS, MAIL_FROM, and MAIL_LIVE_APPROVED=yes (required; live email never starts by default)
#   TRUST_PROXY_HOPS=<number of reverse proxies in front of Express, 0 to 3, default 0>   (per-IP limits read the client address from it)
#   PORT=<optional, default 3000>
# See docs/production-readiness.md.
# Credentials come from Application Default Credentials (e.g. the runtime service account); never commit a key file.
NODE_ENV=development
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=demo-nufv
FIREBASE_AUTH_EMULATOR_HOST=127.0.0.1:9099
FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST=127.0.0.1:8080
PORT=3000
# Live Gmail delivery is OFF here on purpose (sink only). To try it, put the settings in server/.env.local (git-ignored,
# never this file) and run `npm run server:mail`; see docs/gmail-smtp-setup.md. `npm run demo` ignores them.
# VOUCHER_ENCRYPTION_KEY is deliberately unset here: development generates a throwaway key on each start, so vouchers
# issued before a restart show "password unavailable".
